```java
// HikariCP keeps connections open; getConnection() borrows one
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    try (Connection con = dataSource.getConnection()) {
        // ... do one small query; close() returns it to the pool, not destroyed
    }
}
```

*Same loop, but the pooled DataSource avoids 1,000 expensive handshakes.*

