```java
// FRESHER TRAP: manual close. If executeQuery or a getXxx throws,
// the close() lines below never run and the Connection leaks.
Connection con = dataSource.getConnection();
PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement("SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE city = ?");
ps.setString(1, "Pune");
ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery();
while (rs.next()) {
    System.out.println(rs.getInt("id") + ": " + rs.getString("name"));
}
rs.close();   // skipped on exception above
ps.close();   // skipped on exception above
con.close();  // leaked Connection eventually exhausts the pool
```

```java
// FIX: declare resources in the try header. They implement AutoCloseable,
// so Java closes them in reverse order even when an exception is thrown.
String sql = "SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE city = ?";
try (Connection con = dataSource.getConnection();
     PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    ps.setString(1, "Pune");
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) {
        while (rs.next()) {
            System.out.println(rs.getInt("id") + ": " + rs.getString("name"));
        }
    }
}
// ResultSet, then PreparedStatement, then Connection close automatically.
```

*Same query, but the pooled Connection always returns to the pool — no leak path.*

